---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';

const updated = '24 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  path="privacy/"
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the APOLLO Network website handles your data: no cookies, no analytics, no trackers and no third-party scripts."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy, briefly."
    lead="This website does not use cookies, analytics, trackers, advertising pixels or third-party scripts. That is the short version, and it is the whole version."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="split__aside">
        <p class="label">Last updated</p>
        <p class="updated">{updated}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What this site collects</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing, directly. There are no cookies, no analytics, no tracking storage and no
          fingerprinting. Fonts, images and scripts are all served from this site itself, so your
          browser does not contact any other company while you read it.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub processes technical data
          such as IP addresses to deliver pages and keep the service secure. That processing is
          governed by the{' '}
          <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
            rel="noopener noreferrer external"
          >
            GitHub General Privacy Statement
            <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens external site)</span>
          </a>
          .
        </p>

        <h2>If you get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          The contact page never sends data anywhere by itself. Its form prepares a message in your
          own email app; nothing is sent until you press send there. APOLLO Network’s inbox is
          provided by Google (Gmail), so emails you send are processed by Google under its own
          privacy terms. Your message is used only to reply to you, and is not shared or sold.
          Please do not include passwords or sensitive personal information.
        </p>
        <p>
          Public enquiries opened on GitHub are visible to anyone and are governed by GitHub’s
          privacy statement.
        </p>

        <h2>The APOLLO assistant</h2>
        <p>
          The assistant in the corner of each page is a guided helper, not an AI. Its answers are
          built into the page, and nothing you choose in it is sent anywhere. It remembers one thing
          — that you have already seen its greeting — in your browser’s session storage for the
          current tab only, so the greeting does not reappear on every page. That entry is removed
          when you close the tab.
        </p>

        <h2>Leaving the site</h2>
        <p>
          Pages instruct your browser not to send a referrer when you follow a link elsewhere, so
          other sites are not told which page you came from.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this ever changes — for example, if privacy-preserving analytics are introduced — this
          page will be updated first, and will say exactly what is collected and why.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  }

  .prose :global(h2) {
    margin-top: 2em;
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .prose :global(h2:first-child) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
